## 1. Phase 6 Objective – Continuous Monitoring & Health Reporting

Develop a continuous health monitoring and reporting system that maintains long-term astronaut health records and helps authorized medical personnel identify changes throughout a space mission.

The purpose of Phase 6 is to monitor health and environmental information over time, maintain historical records, identify recurring concerns, track individual health patterns and generate periodic reports.

SPACE PULSE must go beyond displaying an astronaut's current health readings.

It should maintain a historical record that allows medical personnel to understand how an astronaut's health and environmental exposure change throughout the mission.

The system must:

- Maintain individual astronaut health records.
- Continuously update health and environmental histories.
- Monitor current physiological readings.
- Monitor current environmental conditions.
- Track individual health trends.
- Track environmental exposure over time.
- Maintain active and previous alert records.
- Identify recurring symptoms.
- Identify repeated environmental concerns.
- Identify potential long-term health deterioration.
- Generate daily, weekly and monthly health reports.
- Generate additional reports when significant changes occur.
- Provide authorized ground medical personnel with access to crew health information.
- Support both individual and crew-wide health reporting.

The system must continue monitoring throughout the mission rather than relying only on occasional health assessments.

