SPACE PULSE must apply appropriate access restrictions.

The system must:

- Provide individual medical records only to authorized personnel.
- Display aggregated crew information in the main crew overview.
- Prevent unauthorized access to individual health records.
- Use existing authentication and authorization mechanisms where available.
- Restrict sensitive report downloads to appropriately authorized users.
- Avoid unnecessarily exposing personal medical information in shared crew reports.

The astronaut and authorized ground medical personnel must have access to information appropriate to their roles.

Do not create unnecessary new authentication systems if the existing application already has authentication and role permissions.

